   286	### 2.3 Dependency and artifact preflight
   287	
   288	On a real cache miss, the fixed `go list` command MUST complete before the
   289	corresponding `go build`. Its complete JSON stream MUST cover the root and every
   290	active dependency, contain exactly one non-`DepOnly` root named `main`, contain
   291	no incomplete result, `Error`, or `DepsErrors`, and select no tests.
   292	
   293	Only a result with both `Standard == true` and `Goroot == true` is a trusted
   294	toolchain package. Its directory and every listed source, module, and embedded
   295	input MUST remain below the fingerprinted `GOROOT`. Every other result, its
   296	package directory, module file, active Go file, and every active embedded input
   297	MUST be a regular file below the command's build root. Escaped, missing,
   298	linked, special, or out-of-root input is rejected.
   299	
   300	Every result MUST have empty `SysoFiles`. Every non-standard result MUST also
   301	have empty `CgoFiles`, `CFiles`, `CXXFiles`, `MFiles`, `HFiles`, `FFiles`,
   302	`SFiles`, `SwigFiles`, and `SwigCXXFiles`. Thus cgo, package-controlled C, C++,
   303	Objective-C, Fortran, assembly, SWIG, and host objects are rejected throughout
   304	the active dependency graph. Each active non-standard `GoFiles` file is scanned
   305	as exact bytes and rejected if it contains `//go:cgo_import_dynamic`. Any
   306	violation fails before `go build`.
   307	
   308	The fixed build forces the native gc compiler, disabled PGO and cgo, and
   309	internal linking with no libgcc. If internal linking cannot produce the output,
   310	the command fails; there is no external-link or libgcc fallback. The only
   311	output is the manager-derived `bin/<command>` or `bin/<command>.exe` at a
   312	bounded regular file in operation staging. The manager hashes it and applies
   313	manager-defined executable permissions but MUST NOT execute it for validation,
   314	version discovery, smoke testing, post-processing, receipt generation,
   315	rollback, repair, or recovery.
   316	
   317	### 2.4 Build cache and dry-run planning
   318	
   319	For each active build command, the manager derives the complete build input,
   320	logical cache key, canonical receipt, receipt hash, and artifact-relative path
   321	exactly as specified by Protocol Core section 9. Persistent reuse is permitted
   322	only below an implementation-specific cache boundary resolved independently of
   323	package input and proven manager-created, manager-owned, privately mutable,
   324	contained, regular-file-only, and link-safe. The manager verifies that boundary
   325	and every entry component on each lookup and again under the manager-home
   326	mutation lock. A manager unable to prove the boundary MUST disable persistent
   327	reuse.
   328	
   329	A candidate hit is accepted only after the manager recomputes build-source
   330	identity, cache key, complete expected input, exact canonical receipt bytes and
   331	hash, manager-derived artifact path, artifact hash, and byte length without
   332	following links or executing the artifact. Unknown fields or unsupported
   333	receipt, driver, build-source, toolchain, or execution-policy identities are
   334	rejected. An entry whose execution policy is absent or differs from the policy
   335	the manager implements is a miss; the manager rebuilds instead of adopting or
   336	upgrading it, and host capability evidence never participates in that
   337	comparison. Internally
   338	consistent bytes outside the protected boundary are not provenance: a real
   339	operation rebuilds from the revalidated snapshot into new protected state,
   340	dry-run reports `would-rebuild-untrusted-cache`, and status is non-current.
   341	
   342	A dry run performs all read-only planning and package-independent toolchain
   343	probes above, rechecks generation digests for every shared target it consulted,
   344	and removes all operation-private state before returning. It reports, per build
   345	command, `cache-hit`, `would-preflight-and-build`,
   346	`would-rebuild-untrusted-cache`, `corrupt`, or `unsupported`. A cache miss is
   347	`would-preflight-and-build` because dry-run MUST NOT run `go list`, `go build`,
