   444	### 2.6 Recovery and repair
   445	
   446	Recovery runs under the manager-home mutation lock before any new shared
   447	mutation. Within install or repair it runs only in the serialized publication
   448	phase after every private build succeeds; it MUST NOT run as a pre-build pass.
   449	It scans every incomplete journal by transaction identifier rather than by the
   450	project that triggered recovery, verifies target preimages and desired digests,
   451	and either completes a wholly uncommitted publication or restores committed
   452	targets in exact reverse order. Backups are retained until recovery or rollback
   453	succeeds. No transaction releases the home lock between its first target swap
   454	and durable success or reverse rollback, so recovery cannot overwrite a later
   455	project's successful commit or lose a consumer-ledger update.
