   649	## 9. Idempotent machine bootstrap
   650	
   651	A manager SHOULD expose a non-interactive operation that creates its machine
   652	configuration only when it is absent. When the configuration path already
   653	exists, this operation MUST succeed without parsing, rewriting, or changing
   654	the existing file. An explicit overwrite operation and create-if-absent mode
   655	MUST be mutually exclusive.
   656	
   657	## 10. Status and garbage collection
   658	
   659	Read-only status validates marker schema, recomputes content hashes, reports
   660	manifest and activation drift, and MAY re-resolve registry attestations. A
   661	check mode returns non-zero for drift without mutating state.
   662	
   663	For a build-enabled marker, status additionally validates static build-root
   664	context exclusion, recomputes `curator-build-source-v1` from the fully validated
   665	raw snapshot, recomputes every build input and logical key, and validates every
   666	referenced receipt and artifact below a currently verified manager-protected
   667	boundary. A missing raw snapshot, context-visible or runtime-copied build-root
   668	file, untrusted boundary, unsupported driver or toolchain, corrupt receipt or
   669	artifact, wrong native target, or source, key, receipt, artifact-path, or
   670	artifact-hash mismatch makes the installation non-current. Status MUST NOT
   671	execute an artifact or mutate, quarantine, repair, or adopt cache state.
   672	
   673	Garbage collection acquires only the manager-home mutation lock and first
   674	revalidates every manager-protected cache boundary it will traverse. It scans
   675	registered consumers and valid markers, marks every runtime and snapshot entry
   676	referenced by an existing consumer, any supported valid marker (currently
   677	marker v1 or marker v2), or an in-flight transaction journal, and marks every
   678	logical build-cache entry referenced by a valid marker v2 or in-flight
   679	transaction journal. It sweeps only unreferenced machine-local entries older
   680	than the manager's documented grace period. Receipt content alone is neither
   681	provenance nor a live reference. An unreadable consumer, marker, journal, or
   682	unprovable cache boundary fails safe: uncertain entries are retained or
   683	conservatively quarantined according to documented local policy and the
   684	uncertainty is reported. GC MUST NOT execute or adopt entry content.
   685	
   686	## 11. External repository manager profile
   687	
   688	This section is the rc.5 manager profile for schema-7
   689	`go-repository-v1` commands. It extends, but does not reinterpret, sections 1
   690	through 10. Schemas 1 through 6, `go-v1`, build receipt schema 1, marker
